# Changelog

## Unreleased

### Added

- Added half-width katakana conversion mappings for `ヰ -> ｲ`, `ヱ -> ｴ`, `ヺ -> ｦﾞ`, and punctuation `。 -> ｡`, `、 -> ､`.
- Added public `destroy()` to the runtime API and synchronized the type declaration.
- Added coverage support in Vitest and quality-gate scripts (`test:coverage`, `ci`).
- Added contributor guidance file (`AGENTS.md`).

### Changed

- Migrated the codebase to TypeScript.
- Changed katakana option design to `katakana: false | 'full' | 'half'` and removed the old `halfWidthKatakana` option.
- Clarified `toKatakana` conversion priority and simplified `setInterval` implementation/readability.
- Updated package metadata for publication readiness (scope, description, repository, bugs, homepage, contributors).
- Aligned type declaration module name with the published package name `@j1nn0/vanilla-autokana`.

### Fixed

- Fixed full-width space normalization so it applies only in half-width katakana mode.
- Applied timer/event lifecycle improvements to avoid stale interval state issues.

### Docs

- Updated README examples to reflect the new katakana API.
- Expanded README and README_en option documentation (`katakana`, `checkInterval`) and framework integration guidance.
- Aligned script-tag examples with `dist/autokana.umd.js`.
- Added clear fork attribution and copyright notes.

### Tests

- Added tests for full-width-space behavior in half-width mode.
- Added integration tests for focus/blur timer lifecycle and keydown conversion reset.
- Improved test readability by fixing misleading variable names in toggle tests.

### Build/Tooling

- Added Vite/Vitest project configuration.
- Updated lint/format tooling configuration (`.oxlintrc.json`, `.oxfmtrc.json`).
- Removed legacy demo files (`autokana.js`, `index.html`).